      "worked": "The common time domain is $0\\leq t\\leq\\sqrt{8}$. For a collision, the displacements must agree.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sqrt{3-t}&=\\sqrt{8-t^2}\\\\4(3-t)&=8-t^2\\\\12-4t&=8-t^2\\\\t^2-4t+4&=0\\\\(t-2)^2&=0\\\\t&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is in the common domain, and $x_A(2)=2\\sqrt{1}=2$ and $x_B(2)=\\sqrt{4}=2$. The particles therefore collide at displacement $x=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}v_A(t)=x_A'(t)&=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-t}}\\\\v_B(t)=x_B'(t)&=-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{8-t^2}}\\\\v_A(2)&=-1\\text{ m s}^{-1}\\\\v_B(2)&=-1\\text{ m s}^{-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nSpeed is the magnitude of velocity, so both particles have speed $1\\text{ m s}^{-1}$ at the collision.",
